window.GLOSS={};
window.EN={"1":"Having lost Agusty, King Chagall moved his court to Madino Castle in the north.","2":"True to his promise with Eldigan, Sigurd did not pursue him.","3":"While resting his troops at Agusty Castle, in order to keep his promise with Eldigan,","4":"Sigurd persistently continued negotiations for the return of Agusty.","5":"But the reply from Belhalla always remained the same: stay in Agusty","6":"and govern the people there.","7":"As half a year passed, the officials sent from Grannvale","8":"came to swagger about Agustrian territory as if it were their own.","9":"The discontent of the people of Agustria swelled little by little.","10":"Eventually, the new war Sigurd had feared broke out.","11":"Chagall, having readied his troops at Madino, tried to retake the capital, Agusty,","12":"and challenged Sigurd to battle.","13":"To the north of Madino, the infamous pirates of Augerhill","14":"were beginning to stir, taking advantage of the war.","15":"The order from Belhalla declared that Agusty Castle must be defended to the last.","16":"Sigurd's heart was heavy as he set out to battle.","17":"To the southwest of Madino, at Silesse Castle, Eldigan's army stood waiting.","18":"This battle might turn him into a betrayer of a friend.","19":"At this time, Sigurd, at the northern edge of Agustria,","20":"was about to face a battle that would change the course of history itself.","21":"Has the army's deployment finished? Make sure they haven't noticed us. Good, then advance as planned.","22":"This is our last chance to take back Agusty.","23":"Those fools, settling into my country so brazenly...","24":"...just you wait. I'll make them eat their words.","25":"Jacobin! Is the swordsman Jacobin here!?","26":"You need me...?","27":"The time has come to see that skill of yours. Defend this castle for me.","28":"Understood... it's a boring job, but it's for the money. This Thunder Sword's terror... I'll show you plenty of it.","29":"That's reassuring. I'm counting on you, Jacobin.","30":"Now then, there's Eldigan at Silesse... that fool, how will he move...","31":"Lord Eldigan, it's terrible! Madino Castle has raised its army!","32":"What, Lord Chagall has!? Damn it... what a rash thing to do! Just when the day I could return to the capital was drawing near...","33":"Ugh... I cannot possibly fight Sigurd. What on earth should I do...","34":"Boss, looks like a war's starting down south. Heh, this is getting interesting.","35":"Let's take advantage of this chance and help ourselves to the village.","36":"Until now Agustria's army was around and we couldn't lift a finger, but now it'll be a cinch.","37":"Hold your tongue, Dovar! If you try pulling some petty thievery, I won't forgive you!","38":"I don't do cheap work like that. It's a matter of principle.","39":"We've made a name for ourselves as righteous bandits—don't disgrace the name of the Augerhill pirates!","40":"Damn it, are you telling us to just sit here twiddling our thumbs while treasure's right there for the taking! The boss is too soft!","41":"Now, now, calm down, Dovar. I have an idea.","42":"That woman isn't really the boss's own daughter, you know.","43":"She was picked up as a kid and raised by the boss on this island.","44":"She thinks she's inherited the position without even knowing that. Well, no need to worry about it.","45":"Let's just help ourselves to the treasure, the two of us.","46":"Lord Sigurd! It's terrible!! King Chagall's army is surrounding this castle!","47":"What! That's absurd... we're about to return home soon, why would we need to fight?","48":"Just what is Eldigan thinking...","49":"On top of that, taking advantage of the chaos, even the Augerhill pirates have started moving.","50":"I see... it can't be helped. Let's march out.","51":"My love... another battle, is it?","52":"Indeed, Deirdre, I'm sorry, but this time I can't take you with me.","53":"I can't leave Celice, who was just born, behind.","54":"Yes...","55":"Don't make such an anxious face. I'll be back soon, I promise.","56":"Right, Shanan, I'll ask this of you—protect Deirdre and Celice for me.","57":"Sure! Don't worry, I'll protect Deirdre, so Sigurd, go on ahead with peace of mind!","58":"Haha, Shanan's always so full of energy.","59":"Deirdre, this should ease your worries a little, at least.","60":"Don't worry. This isn't a permanent parting, you know.","61":"Lord Sigurd...","62":"[Only if neither Lex nor Ayra has a sweetheart, and the Horin-Ayra scene hasn't been seen]","63":"Hey, Ayra.","64":"Lex, is it... what do you want?","65":"Tch, as unfriendly as ever.","66":"I'm busy. If you have no business with me, go away.","67":"Wait up, I got something good and thought I'd give it to you.","68":"If it's a gift, give it to some other woman. I have no interest in things like that.","69":"Heh heh, even this?","70":"Hm? ...Ah! That's...","71":"That's right, it's a famous sword called the Hero's Blade. You must've at least heard the name.","72":"This is the Hero's Blade... what a beautiful sword...","73":"Seems you like it. Go on, take it, here.","74":"Ah, wait, Lex!","75":"Lex...","76":"[Only if neither Horin nor Ayra has a sweetheart, and the Lex-Ayra scene hasn't been seen]","77":"Ayra, take this sword.","78":"Isn't this the Hero's Blade? Why give it to me? You should use it yourself.","79":"I have a feeling this is going to be a tough battle. For a fighter with a style like yours, there's no such thing as too many swords.","80":"Use it to protect yourself. I can't always be there to help you, after all.","81":"Horin... thank you. I'll put it to good use.","82":"Oh, you've come to help us! Then this village's people will be saved too.","83":"It's not much of a thank-you, but please accept this magic staff.","84":"This is called the Restore Staff—it can undo conditions like Sleep or Silence.","85":"I'm sure it will come in handy.","86":"[Before Silesse Castle is subdued]","87":"The Cross Knights are the elite order of knights led by Lord Eldigan—said to be the finest in the whole continent.","88":"Actually, you know, my boyfriend is a member of the Cross Knights too. Heh heh, isn't that amazing?","89":"[After Silesse Castle is subdued]","90":"Ohhh, my boyfriend died in this war.","91":"This is all because of the Grannvale army... no, it's because of King Chagall!","92":"How could the Augerhill pirates do something this awful, of all things...","93":"We trusted that woman boss, Brigid!","94":"Ho ho, well, thank you for coming. As thanks, I'll give you this sword.","95":"This is called the Swallow Strike—a magic sword that deals a critical blow to anything that flies.","96":"If you can't use it, you could sell it.","97":"Oh, you've come a long way. It's not much of a thank-you, but please take this village's secret medicine.","98":"Here, drink up.","99":"There now, don't you feel strength surging through your body? This should let you work even harder.","100":"Watch out—there's a rumor that King Chagall has hired the Dragon Knights of Thracia.","101":"They say those fellows get hired by whichever side pays, whenever a war breaks out, and kill indiscriminately.","102":"Just like hyenas feeding on carrion...","103":"Hah, take this! Thunder Sword!","104":"Gah, how... unfortunate...","105":"Lord Sigurd, King Chagall is nowhere to be seen.","106":"I see... he's probably fled to Silesse. Eldigan is at that castle.","107":"His Cross Knights are Agustria's last remaining military strength.","108":"If only he'd sheathe his sword here and let it end...","109":"Lord Sigurd, Father Claude of Edda has come to visit.","110":"What!? Lord Claude has... bring him in at once.","111":"Lord Sigurd, it's been a while. I've come to speak with you—the truth is, something terrible has happened back home.","112":"Why, Father Claude, whatever could have happened?","113":"Prince Kurth was murdered by someone on his way back from the campaign.","114":"What!? No way... who on earth would kill Lord Kurth!","115":"Lord Byron was always at Prince Kurth's side...","116":"But he's been nowhere to be seen since the day the prince was murdered. This is hard to say, but...","117":"Suspicion for the prince's murder has fallen on Lord Byron... that is, on your own father...","118":"Wh-what did you say!? That's absurd!","119":"All sorts of baseless rumors are circulating back home.","120":"Some even say that you and Lord Byron conspired together to kill the prince...","121":"His Majesty has collapsed from the grief of it all.","122":"My father was the one the prince trusted most. What could he possibly gain from doing away with the prince?","123":"Shouldn't suspicion fall on the two dukes said to oppose the prince—Reptor and Langobalt?","124":"I think so too, but there's no proof.","125":"Right now the court is dominated by the Reptor faction.","126":"What does Lord Arvis, His Majesty's close aide, think about this?","127":"I don't really understand what that man thinks. I don't believe he's hostile to you, but whether he's an ally... that I don't know.","128":"I see... I'm worried about my father too.","129":"I want to return home right away, but His Majesty has ordered me to defend this land, so I can't.","130":"Father Claude, what should I do?","131":"I intend to go now to the Tower of Baldr on the northwestern island.","132":"If I, a descendant of the holy Baldr, pray at that sacred tower, the whole truth should come to light.","133":"I intend to tell His Majesty everything. Lord Sigurd, please rest easy.","134":"Father Claude, stop dawdling and let's go already, I'm bored.","135":"Oh? You're Tiltyu of House Freege. Why are you with Father Claude?","136":"Because the father's all alone and that's worrying, isn't it? I'm the one protecting him.","137":"But you're the daughter of Duke Reptor...","138":"I don't understand difficult things, but I love the father!","139":"Honestly... this child is a handful... in any case, once the truth is known, I'll join your forces.","140":"Let's go home together.","141":"Understood, Father Claude. I'm counting on you.","142":"Shanan, I hear Lord Sigurd has taken Madino Castle. I'm going to go see him once.","143":"No way, Deirdre, it's still dangerous outside! And what about Celice?","144":"That's why I want to ask you to look after Celice.","145":"No way, I don't wanna, taking care of a baby isn't a man's job!","146":"Please, I'll be right back, Shanan, please...","147":"Tch, fine, I get it. Go on then. But come back soon, okay?","148":"Thank you, Shanan. Celice, I'm sorry, I'll be back soon.","149":"...I've finally found you... daughter of Sigyun...","150":"Huh, who are you? ...How do you know my mother's name...","151":"Kukuku... you are about to be reborn...","152":"By my dark magic, you will lose all your memories and become some man's wife...","153":"That is your fate. Give up...","154":"Wh-what are you doing!? ...Stop it!! ...Ahh... Sigur... d...","155":"What have you been doing, Eldigan! While you dawdled, even Madino has been taken!","156":"So then, you, in league with the enemy, mean to destroy this country?","157":"Your Majesty... you would say such a thing to me!","158":"What, are you dissatisfied?","159":"Forgetting the debt you owe my father, dragging your feet to buy time—can a man like that really be called a knight!","160":"It seems nothing I say will do any good anymore. Understood, Lord Chagall. We will sortie.","161":"I too am a proud Holy Knight of Agustria. If I'm to fall either way, I'd rather fall fighting.","162":"Your Majesty, I leave the rest in your hands.","163":"The time to sortie has finally come. This may be the last time we all meet alive.","164":"I will never forget the loyalty you have all shown until now.","165":"This is a battle that wagers our homeland's very survival. Fight your fullest, as knights should. Cross Knights, sortie!","166":"That Eldigan, finally sortied, has he... taking his sweet time...","167":"Those who remain, firm up the castle's defenses! From now on, I will take command of you all myself.","168":"Eldigan, I beg you! Lower your sword! I don't want to fight you!","169":"I will fulfill my promise to return Agusty, even at the cost of my life. Just trust me a little longer!","170":"...Sigurd, I'm sorry, say no more.","171":"At this point, all that's left is to fight a battle we need not be ashamed of, as fellow knights.","172":"Now then, let's go, Sigurd! My magic sword Mystletainn—will it defeat you!?","173":"Brother! It's me, Lachesis! Please, stop this meaningless battle.","174":"Are you betraying Lord Sigurd!? Is betraying a friend a knight's pride!?","175":"Brother! Trust Lord Sigurd and hold off on this battle, even just a little longer.","176":"Lachesis... don't cry like that, there's no other way left.","177":"If I lose Lord Chagall, Agustria will be destroyed.","178":"No, brother, if only Lord Chagall would withdraw his army,","179":"Lord Sigurd has no intention of continuing this fight.","180":"Please, I beg you—Lord Chagall surely can't ignore the words of you, who leads the Cross Knights.","181":"......Understood, Lachesis. I'll try persuading His Majesty once more.","182":"If I'm to risk the same life either way, the knight's way of living is to fight for a friend, not an unwilling battle.","183":"Lachesis... I'll give this sword to you.","184":"This is... the Earth Sword!? ...Brother! No way!!","185":"If something happens to me, think of it as a keepsake. Lachesis, don't you dare die!","186":"Ahh, wait! Brother Elt!!","187":"Your Majesty, this battle is pointless beyond this point. Please withdraw the troops.","188":"Agusty will surely return to your hands someday.","189":"Eldigan, you! Coming back now and spouting such things! So you really were colluding with the enemy after all!","190":"Someone, seize that traitor! I'll have his head cut off and put on display!","191":"So it really was useless after all... too bad, but this is the end for Agustria too...","192":"Heh, you fool, so you've resigned yourself to it. Fine, I don't care, cut him down right here.","193":"Lachesis......!","194":"Ah, well, you've come a long way. Drink this magic medicine, it'll raise your defenses a bit.","195":"Do you wish to become prey to this magic sword, Mystletainn,","196":"Those who don't want to die, do not come near me......!","197":"Forgive me, people of Agustria......","198":"Why, why did I have to kill Eldigan... just what am I fighting for, after all...","199":"Lord Sigurd, please, don't blame yourself.","200":"For now, please carry on Lord Eldigan's dying wish and restore peace for Agustria's people as soon as possible.","201":"Travant, are the Dragon Knights ready?","202":"No need to worry. For the money I was paid, I'll work.","203":"Hmph, more useful than my spineless vassals, mercenaries who work for money, aren't they?","204":"I'm counting on you!","205":"Hurry, Agustria is right before us!","206":"This time the enemy is Grannvale. Fight to your heart's content and make the name of the Kingdom of Thracia ring out across the world!","207":"Fufufu, know the terror of the Dragon Knights, prepare yourself!","208":"Ugh......glory to Thracia......!","209":"Tch, Papillon's failed, has he. This is a good time to pull back. I have no obligation to go down with Agustria.","210":"Farewell, foolish King Chagall.","211":"Wh-what are you, you rabble! I am the King of Agustria! You insolent fools!","212":"Damn it... I'll strike you down myself!","213":"My... my Agustria......","214":"Eldigan...","215":"Lord Sigurd, please, don't let your spirits fall.","216":"Also, I'm sorry to bring this up at a time like this, but it seems Shanan has come from Agusty Castle.","217":"He says he has something he wants to tell you...","218":"Shanan is...?","219":"Sigurd, I'm sorry, I'm so sorry.","220":"What's wrong, I can't understand you if you just cry. What happened?","221":"Deirdre went out and hasn't come back. She said she was going to see Sigurd...","222":"I'm sorry, it was my promise to protect her.","223":"What! Deirdre's...!! Then what about Celice... what happened to my son?","224":"I kept Celice with me, look, he's right here. But Deirdre...","225":"...I see... understood, Shanan, it's not your fault. Don't worry about it anymore, I'll go search for Deirdre myself.","226":"But, if only I'd stopped her more firmly... I'm sorry, Sigurd.","227":"Deirdre... just where on earth are you...","228":"Boss! Agustria's lost!","229":"The Grannvale lot might come attack us too. What should we do?","230":"Dovar! In the first place, it's because you lot raided a village without telling me, isn't it!","231":"I won't forgive you! You lot!!","232":"Keh, quit it already!! Get complacent if we go easy on you for once!","233":"You're not really the former boss's true daughter, you know.","234":"The boss picked up a crying kid from a raided ship and raised her, that's all.","235":"And that brat has the nerve to order us around—how laughable.","236":"Wh-what are you saying... that's not...","237":"Anyway, we've got no more use for you. Time to die.","238":"Damn it, you think I'll just go down that easily!","239":"You lot, finish off that woman! Don't let her get away!","240":"Pisarr, I'm heading back to the castle. You lead the men and go pillage Agustria.","241":"Right, got it!","242":"Good, lower the bridge! Agustria is ours now!!","243":"Father Claude, hurry, hurry!! Isn't the prayer already over?","244":"If you dawdle in a place like that, the pirates will find us and we'll get killed!","245":"Yes yes, Tiltyu, I'm coming now. The prayer to the god Baldr revealed the whole truth.","246":"Just as I thought, it was exactly as I suspected.","247":"And what's more, I was able to find the lost holy relic, the Valkyrie Staff.","248":"Here, take a look.","249":"What's that dirty-looking staff?","250":"...Tiltyu, you'll be struck by divine punishment for saying such things.","251":"This staff can bring the dead back to life.","252":"Only I, a descendant of the saint Baldr, can use it.","253":"Huh, really? Then can that grandma I liked come back to life too?","254":"Unfortunately, it's not that simple. There are various restrictions, so it's not something that works for just anyone.","255":"Humans each have something called life-force, which they're born with...","256":"Ehh... Father's talk is too hard, it's making me yawn.","257":"Anyway, who cares about that, let's hurry and run.","258":"Yes, you're right, let's flee.","259":"Quan... there's something I need to apologize to you for...","260":"Huh? What's wrong, Ethlyn, making such a serious face?","261":"This...","262":"Hm...!? Th-this is the Gae Bolg lance, isn't it! How do you have this...","263":"I was entrusted with it by Father. If the fighting ever got intense, I was to hand it to you.","264":"I see, having this lance would be a great help. But why have you kept silent about it until now?","265":"Because I heard the legend of this lance from Father... I'm sorry...","266":"...A sad tale about Gae Bolg, is it... but I don't believe in it. That's just a legend, nothing more.","267":"But...","268":"Ethlyn, trust me. Victory is near. And then let's go home to Leonster together.","269":"I can't leave little Altena alone forever, after all.","270":"Yes... but Quan... no matter what happens, we'll stay together, won't we...","271":"Are you thinking about Deirdre... don't worry, she'll be found soon, I'm sure.","272":"Yeah... I want to believe that too, but... still...","273":"Ethlyn? Are you crying? Do you have a bad feeling about something?","274":"It feels like the two of them might never meet again...","275":"They loved each other so much, so why... Quan...","276":"Ethlyn...","277":"Are you all right, Brigid?","278":"Who are you? How do you know my name?","279":"I heard it from the villagers—they say the woman boss of the Augerhill pirates protected the powerless.","280":"That must be you.","281":"I see... so you're Sigurd of Grannvale... well then, there's nothing for it. If you're going to kill me, go ahead.","282":"Hahaha, seems you've got the wrong idea. I've come to invite you.","283":"What do you say, won't you come with us? I want to borrow your strength.","284":"You want to invite someone like me?","285":"That's right, I want you.","286":"Lord Sigurd... you're an odd one...","287":"[Only if neither Mideel nor Brigid has a sweetheart]","288":"Lady Edain...?","289":"Hm? Who are you? I don't know you at all.","290":"So you're not Lady Edain after all... but how could this be...","291":"What a strange one. What's he muttering about...","292":"What's your name...","293":"Brigid, that's my name...","294":"Brigid... what a beautiful person...","295":"Wh-what did you say! Are you mocking me!?","296":"To think there was someone more beautiful than her... unbelievable...","297":"I... I'm leaving now...","298":"You are... after all, Big Sister! Brigid, it's me, your little sister Edain!","299":"Please, try to remember.","300":"How do you know my name... and besides, your face looks just like mine.","301":"......Edain... I feel like I have heard that before...","302":"I am your twin sister. Big Sister, you were taken away by pirates at the age of five.","303":"I've been searching for you this whole time.","304":"But I can't believe it so suddenly. Do you have any proof?","305":"Then please, try drawing this bow.","306":"Hm? It's quite a fine bow, but what of it?","307":"I just draw it...? Wh-what is this... what's happening...","308":"! ...Some strange power is filling up inside me... my memories... are coming back...","309":"Ahh... my chest feels hot... Edain, you are Edain... my little sister...","310":"I'm so glad... you remember now. That bow has been passed down in our family—the god-bow Yewfelle.","311":"It's said that only a direct descendant can wield a divine weapon.","312":"In our family, that's only you, Big Sister Brigid. That's the best proof there could be.","313":"Edain... ahh... let me get a good look at your face... is Father well?","314":"What about my brother... Andrey...","315":"I have so much to tell you too, Big Sister...","316":"Lord Sigurd! I've finally met you!","317":"Father Claude! You're safe!! I was so worried when I heard the pirates had attacked you.","318":"Yes, thanks to Tiltyu, I somehow managed to get through it.","319":"More importantly, Lord Sigurd, the prayer at Baldr succeeded.","320":"You learned the truth!?","321":"Yes, it was indeed Lord Reptor's plot after all. He used Langobalt to kill Prince Kurth","322":"and pinned the crime on your father, Lord Byron.","323":"So it really was that, after all!","324":"Yes, and it was also Lord Reptor's doing that killed King Mannanan of Isaach.","325":"Fearing he'd lose his pretext for conquering Isaach, he secretly killed King Mannanan.","326":"So that's how it was... so everything was Reptor's doing after all...","327":"No, it's not just his ambition alone. Something truly terrifying seems to be lurking behind it.","328":"There exists some wicked consciousness so great that even the god Baldr cannot see through it...","329":"A wicked consciousness... could it be the Dark Church... Father Claude, then what about my father!?","330":"It seems he hasn't passed away, but the thread of his life could snap at any moment...","331":"Father... no, it can't be...","332":"I'll hurry back to the capital and report the truth to His Majesty.","333":"Lord Sigurd, please wait here. You mustn't act rashly.","334":"Yes, I understand.","335":"Father Claude, please, I beg you—please clear my father's disgraced name somehow.","336":"Yes, everything is as God wills it...","337":"Another war has started, how awful.","338":"Agustria and Grannvale mean nothing to the likes of us.","339":"If they're going to fight a war, I wish they'd do it somewhere else.","340":"Oh! So this is the Tower of Baldr. Heh heh, my thieving spirit is tingling. I wonder if there's anything good...","341":"Hmm, there's nothing here at all... what about over there...","342":"...No good, there's nothing... who are you...","343":"Eh...!? What business do you have at the Tower of Baldr...","344":"I'll pretend I didn't hear that... I will not forgive those who defile this holy ground. Leave......!","345":"Yikes!! Please forgive me!","346":"Whew, that scared me... huh? There's a sword lying around in a place like this.","347":"Hmm, let me take a quick look around... I'll just take this.","348":"What do I care if it's the Grannvale army! I'll have you enjoy the terror of the Augerhill pirates to the fullest!","349":"Damn it... there's no way the Augerhill pirates could lose...","350":"Damn it, every single one of you is useless!","351":"Dammit......","352":"The pirates' castle has been subdued.","353":"Oifey, tell the whole army to gather. I'm worried whether everyone's safe.","354":"Yes, Lord Sigurd.","355":"Now then, I declare to the whole army: seize the traitor Sigurd and his band!","356":"They conspired with Byron to kill Prince Kurth, and tried to make the kingdom their own.","357":"This is His Majesty's order! Show no mercy to those who defy the nation!!","358":"Kukuku, even Langobalt is being quite shameless...","359":"Even while hurting Byron, who resisted after killing the prince with his own hands,","360":"to think he can say such things... but that Arvis, taking advantage of His Majesty's deep trust in him,","361":"spun a fine story, didn't he. In the first place, if we're talking about who planned all this, it was him,","362":"and yet he's pinning the blame entirely on House Sylvail.","363":"Heh heh, well, it's fine. As long as we can each become king of a country as promised, that's good enough.","364":"Troublesome people must be made to disappear...","365":"What's this! I'm the traitor...?","366":"You mean to say a great army has come from Grannvale to capture me!?","367":"Lord Sigurd...... just as the fighting finally ended, right when we were about to go search for Lady Deirdre...","368":"Ugh... has His Majesty really believed Reptor and the others' words?","369":"Did he really believe that my father killed Prince Kurth?","370":"Ahh, if only I'd waited at least until Father Claude returned.","371":"Just what have I been fighting for, to the point of letting Eldigan die!","372":"Lord Sigurd......","373":"Lord Sigurd, I am a knight of Silesse, Mahnya.","374":"By order of Queen Lahna, I have come to escort you.","375":"Please, withdraw to Silesse for now. Please wait in Silesse until the time comes to restore your honor.","376":"...Silesse's Queen Lahna?","377":"Betrayed by my own homeland, and now Silesse would save me?","378":"Lord Sigurd, there's no time. Grannvale's pursuit will begin before long.","379":"The Pegasus Knights will cross the sea and escort you all the way to Silesse."};
